{
  "id": "21435_hitan",
  "headword": "{悲嘆|ひたん}",
  "reading": "ひたん",
  "romaji": "hitan",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "grief; sorrow; lamentation",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "grief, sorrow, lamentation",
      "explanation": "Deep sadness and emotional pain, especially caused by loss, misfortune, or the state of the world. A literary and formal word for grief."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "21435_hitan_ex1",
      "japanese": "{悲嘆|ひたん}に{暮|く}れる。",
      "english": "To be overwhelmed with grief.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21435_hitan_ex2",
      "japanese": "{彼女|かのじょ}は{夫|おっと}の{死|し}を{深|ふか}く{悲嘆|ひたん}した。",
      "english": "She grieved deeply over her husband's death.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21435_hitan_ex3",
      "japanese": "{突然|とつぜん}の{事故|じこ}で{息子|むすこ}を{失|うしな}った{母親|ははおや}は、{深|ふか}い{悲嘆|ひたん}の{中|なか}にいた。",
      "english": "The mother who lost her son in a sudden accident was in deep grief.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A compound of {悲|ひ} (sad) and {嘆|たん} (to sigh, to lament). More literary and formal than {悲|かな}しみ. The verb form is {悲嘆|ひたん}する. Often used in written language, news, and formal contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {悲嘆|ひたん}に{暮|く}れる: to be consumed by grief\n- {悲嘆|ひたん}に{沈|しず}む: to sink into sorrow\n- {深|ふか}い{悲嘆|ひたん}: deep grief\n- {悲嘆|ひたん}の{涙|なみだ}: tears of grief\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {悲|かな}しみ: sadness — the everyday word for sadness, broader and less intense\n- {哀悼|あいとう}: mourning, condolence — specifically grief expressed for the dead\n- {嘆|なげ}き: lamentation, grief — somewhat literary but less formal than {悲嘆|ひたん}",
